                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.34347/2611.34347v1/fig_teaser.png",
                "caption": "Figure 1:AIRIS: evaluating social embodied intelligence over time.An egocentric episode illustrates four linked capabilities: grounding social cues (Attention), inferring the partner’s goal (Intention), deciding Ego’s response (Reaction), and evaluating the exchange (Interaction). Each query uses only observations up to the query time, without access to future evidence.",
                "position": 283
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "header": "2The AIRIS Benchmark",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.34347/2611.34347v1/fig_data_pipeline.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:AIRIS construction pipeline.Web videos are screened, human-verified, and segmented into episodes. Clips then receive fully manual Attention labels and model-assisted, multi-annotator Intention, Reaction, and Interaction labels with group adjudication. Verified A-I-R-I annotations are templated into a candidate question pool and expert-curated into the final benchmark.",
                "position": 740
            }
        ]
    },
